<title>MEXICO: Mexico says to begin avocado talks with Israel.</title>
<headline>Mexico says to begin avocado talks with Israel.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican and Israeli avocado exporters agreed to begin talks on sales of the fruit to Europe, a Mexican official said here on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We agreed to form a commission between the two countries, Mexico and Israel, and we will possibly invite South Africa,&quot; director of the Mexican Association of Avocado Exporters, Ricardo Salgado, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said Spain could also be invited to the meeting slated to be held by June 22.</p>
<p>Israel is one of Europe's leading providers of avocados. Mexico has recently made inroads to attack the European market, the world's top market with 78 percent of imports, Salgado said.</p>
<p>Mexico exported 33,730 tonnes of the fruit in the 1996-1997 season, an increase of 32.7 percent from the previous harvest, he aded.</p>
<p>World avocado exports have quadrupled in the past 15 years to about two million tonnes per year currently.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397))</p>
